{
  "$comment": "The 23 global type styles (EDITOR-ARCHITECTURE.md §4.1). Single source for the Typography panels of config/settings_schema.json (manifests/theme-settings.json), the option list of the per-element type fragment (fragments/type.json) and the designed values that snippets/css-variables.liquid emits as --t-<id>-* tokens (its TYPE_STYLES table must equal this file; the T1.1 token-math proof checks it). desktop/mobile are the asset CSS expressions verbatim (assets/base.css + base-pages.css); hs = --heading-scale, bs = --body-scale, live 110 % / 90 %. breakpoint = the verbatim media query inside which css-variables switches --t-<id>-size to --t-<id>-size-m (and -lh to -lh-m): the query the style's elements use today for their phone size, or (max-width: 749px), the theme's phone query, when the style keeps one size everywhere; null = no switch. swap false = the phone size is never switched on :root (wordmark: its phone size reaches the logo only through --bar-logo, §4.1). elements: the selectors that wear the style today; token_props = the properties whose asset value equals the style token at defaults (bind those to --t-<id>-*); keeps = the properties whose asset value differs from the token (bind them without the token, or keep them out of the binding); inherits = properties the selector does not declare (nothing to bind). Info strings are measured at 1440px wide with the live global sizes.",
